+  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- perf log
+  // All perf state lives inside one JS object. Writing to a QML *property*
+  // from inside dmenuRowListHeight() would make it a dependency of the
+  // visibleRowsHeight binding and produce a binding loop, so mutate the
+  // object's fields instead — that emits no change notification.
+  // ------------------------------------------------- rows-height suspension
+  //
+  // visibleRowsHeight binds to displayModel.count, and both height functions
+  // walk every row in the model. Filling the model therefore costs O(rows²):
+  // a 231-row dmenu ran 234 height passes over ~27k rows — 111ms of a 134ms
+  // open, measured with OMARCHY_MENU_PERF=1. Appending the rows in one
+  // append(array) call does not help: the model still emits a count change
+  // per row.
+  //
+  // So suspend the height instead. While `suspendRowsHeight` is true the
+  // functions hand back the last computed value, which makes every
+  // intermediate evaluation O(1); clearing the flag at the end of a rebuild
+  // triggers exactly one real pass. The cache lives in a JS object rather
+  // than a QML property because writing a property from inside the binding
+  // would make it a dependency of visibleRowsHeight and loop.
+  property bool suspendRowsHeight: false
+  readonly property var rowsHeightCache: ({ value: 0 })
+
